# Emberwake environment
#
# There are NO required environment variables. Clone the repository, install and
# run: the local adapter embeds Postgres, so `npm run dev` works with zero setup
# and creates its own schema and demo seed on first request.
#
# The variables below are only needed to point a deployment at hosted storage.

# --- Datastore -------------------------------------------------------------
# Hosted Postgres connection string. In production this is REQUIRED: a production
# build with no DATABASE_URL deliberately reports itself as degraded rather than
# silently falling back to a local file.
#
#   Neon (recommended):  https://console.neon.tech -> create a project -> copy the
#                       pooled connection string
#   Any Postgres 14+:    postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require
#
# Never commit a real value. `.env*` is git-ignored.
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://..."

# --- Canonical origin ------------------------------------------------------
# The deployed origin, used for canonical URLs, Open Graph tags and the QR codes
# that point at the join page. Defaults to https://emberwake-lyart.vercel.app.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://your-deployment.example.com"

# --- Nothing else ----------------------------------------------------------
# Emberwake deliberately has no API-key environment variables.
#   * Open-Meteo sunrise/sunset and geocoding require no key.
#   * Whisper speech-to-text is an open-weight model downloaded by the player's
#     own browser and executed locally; no inference server and no credentials.